<!--Post: 4668--><!--Time: 1106654162-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4668"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 3:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;ve been studying the BTK story for a few months and like everyone else, have some strong gut feelings I would like to share.  First, this is my initial post - so please forgive mistakes I may make in ignorance. <BR> <BR>BTK is probably nothing like the picture he portrayed in the clues he sent.  Each and everyone is an attempt to throw investigators off his scent.  My estimate is that he is in his mid to late fifties, average height, slightly overweight, glasses, greying and non-descript for all purposes. <BR> <BR>BTK was not born or raised in KS.  He came here for the aviation work and at first, when he was in his early twenties, he was angry over a failed marriage.  This would be when he killed the Otero&#39;s.  I think he knew them from some sort of martial arts group.  I heard they were into Judo, or another grappling art.  Knowing the father could overpower him, BTK entered the home when Joe was gone - and subdued the mother and kids, using them as threat against Joe when he returned. <BR> <BR>I think BTK enjoyed the &#34;power&#34; of the kill. I doubt he was ever interested in the sexual aspect - or had any pedophile tendencies.   <BR> <BR>BTK then remarried - a woman who was intellectually his lesser.  He probably had kids and was a good father.  He would be a little strict with a boy - but probably very lenient with a girl - she could wrap him around her little finger...   <BR> <BR>Children are important to BTK.  He sees what he did as &#34;holy&#34; in some way - as if he was given, or entrusted with, a special gift, directly from God - to kill - and that God did not hold this against him.  I would also offer that BTK after his second marriage, entered some sort of &#39;religious era&#39;.  Probably evangelical - because that supports a man controlling his household.  He would have looked for verification of his acts in the life and values he built for himself.  I doubt that he thinks most women are his equal - he would like a return to the McCarthyistic era in that sense.   <BR> <BR>His wife would have to be a &#39;doormat&#39;.  They would have set up privacy rules - and she would have followed them explicitly - never looking in his things - or reading his notes, etc.  Using religion - he enforced this - and she never suspected. <BR> <BR>But, he changed late in 2003 - I don&#39;t think it was a physical change - but a mental, emotional, or spiritual one.   <BR> <BR>His wife would be in the time of her life that signals the end of child-bearing and that could be an impetus for his restlessness.  He closely associates the need to &#39;bring children into the world&#39; with his ability to &#39;take them out&#39;.  Losing that option would make his wife less physically attractive, intimacy probably declined sharply, and they may sleep in separate rooms now - or they may have divorced.   <BR> <BR>At this point - I think he is harmless.  He would use the knowledge that he is &#39;different&#39; from other SK&#39;s by the fact that he quit killing when the experts say a SK can not quit.  It empowers him - and he justifies his actions in that.  It makes him feel &#39;special&#39; in some way.  He&#39;s not a SK - because he quit.  That&#39;s what he thinks, anyway.   <BR> <BR>I doubt he feels guilty about his crimes - maybe he is sorry for the pain caused to family members - but he views his victims as &#34;collateral damage&#34; in some greater sphere.  I&#39;ll bet he knows the Bible backwards and forewards. <BR> <BR>He probably had some military training - as many have mentioned - but he did not fight in a war - probably used his time to get money for college - he started before his first youthful marriage - finished after that split.   <BR> <BR>He is an avid reader - writes well, English is his first language - and the only thing that reveals the real BTK in his correspondence - is his poetry. <BR> <BR>Not what he wrote - but &#39;because&#39; he wrote it.  Poets are &#39;feelers&#39; - BTK feels things deeply.   <BR> <BR>BTK in his middle age years may have joined some &#34;control&#34; groups, PAC&#39;s, and the like.  He is probably Republican, a white-collar job involving computers, and he would be attracted to groups that tried to, &#34;keep gays out of BoyScouts&#34;, or &#34;ban abortion&#34;, or &#34;close the borders&#34;, things of that nature as they are a harmless extension and outlet for his &#39;control&#39; aspect. <BR> <BR>BTK may continue to reveal clues - but he may also &#34;move on&#34; - this cycle of life ending - he may try something else - in another area - or employer.  I think it is a toss-up at this point.  His kids would be adults - or close, by now, and with his wife&#39;s fertility ending - he is once again, looking for something to fill that &#39;void&#39;. <BR> <BR>So he is dangling the carrot - but he may not drop it.  He knows the PD has nothing on him - and he is enjoying this time to &#39;rub it in&#39;.   <BR> <BR>The bogus arrest a month or so ago - would have greatly pumped his ego.  All his BS was actually believed - and the PD went after someone matching the clues BTK sent in.  He probably laughed - or got a rush out of it - for days.   <BR> <BR>He feels invincible.   <BR> <BR>Those are my, somewhat disconnected thoughts this early morning.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
