<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4698"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 25, 2005 - 1:20 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><font color="0000ff">Hi Tippy,</font> <BR><font color="0000ff">Thanks for time you spent in creating a theory. To make things easier, I&#39;ll give you my thoughts by using this blue text. One thing: We  have a professional criminologist and profiler on this board. His detailed profile has almost always been on the money. I say this in case you haven&#39;t read Dr. Kelleher&#39;s profile <i>and</i> his answers to questions.</font> <BR> <BR>I&#39;ve been studying the BTK story for a few months and like everyone else, have some strong gut feelings I would like to share. First, this is my initial post - so please forgive mistakes I may make in ignorance.  <BR> <BR>BTK is probably nothing like the picture he portrayed in the clues he sent.<font color="0000ff">I agree completely.</font> Each and everyone is an attempt to throw investigators off his scent. My estimate is that he is in his mid to late fifties, average height, slightly overweight, glasses, greying and non-descript for all purposes. <font color="0000ff">BTK has been able to almost flawlessly blend in, regardless of the situation. I agree he&#39;d be considered at least somewhat non-descript by the few who know him. He is shrewd and knows the city of Wichita like the back of his hand.</font> <BR> <BR>BTK was not born or raised in KS.<font color="0000ff">Perhaps not born in Kansas but I believe brought up there.</font> He came here for the aviation work and at first, when he was in his early twenties, he was angry over a failed marriage.<font color="0000ff">This is possible. I don&#39;t quite see this being the case but it&#39;s a plausible scenario.</font> This would be when he killed the Otero&#39;s. I think he knew them from some sort of martial arts group. I heard they were into Judo, or another grappling art. Knowing the father could overpower him, BTK entered the home when Joe was gone - and subdued the mother and kids,<font color="0000ff">In my opinion, BTK thought both of the kids would be in school: I firmly believe Mrs. Julie Otero was the BTK&#39;s prime target.</font> using them as threat against Joe when he returned.  <BR> <BR>I think BTK enjoyed the &#34;power&#34; of the kill.<font color="0000ff">Without question. Power and control are embedded fiercely in BTK&#39;s psyche.</font> I doubt he was ever interested in the sexual aspect - or had any pedophile tendencies. <font color="0000ff">It seems to me that BTK did have some sexual interest in the killings, but control was even more important. I agree that BTK was not a pedophile.</font> <BR> <BR>BTK then remarried - a woman who was intellectually his lesser. He probably had kids and was a good father. He would be a little strict with a boy - but probably very lenient with a girl - she could wrap him around her little finger... <font color="0000ff">One never knows but if he has kids, I doubt he&#39;s a good father - most sociopath&#39;s aren&#39;t - and I have to respectfully but sharply disagree with BTK being lenient toward any female, including a daughter, supposing he even has one.</font> <BR> <BR>Children are important to BTK. He sees what he did as &#34;holy&#34; in some way - as if he was given, or entrusted with, a special gift, directly from God - to kill - and that God did not hold this against him.<font color="0000ff">I understand what you mean; but while BTK has an unrealistically high opinion of himself I would also offer that BTK has never been deeply involved in religion of any kind.</font>second marriage, entered some sort of &#39;religious era&#39;. Probably evangelical - because that supports a man controlling his household. He would have looked for verification of his acts in the life and values he built for himself. I doubt that he thinks most women are his equal - he would like a return to the McCarthyistic era in that sense. <font color="0000ff">I think your last sentence is a bullseye.</font> <BR> <BR>His wife would have to be a &#39;doormat&#39;. They would have set up privacy rules - and she would have followed them explicitly - never looking in his things - or reading his notes, etc. Using religion - he enforced this - and she never suspected. <font color="0000ff">Only BTK knows but again, I don&#39;t see any serious religiousness in any aspect of BTK&#39;s adult life.</font> <BR> <BR>But, he changed late in 2003 - I don&#39;t think it was a physical change - but a mental, emotional, or spiritual one. <font color="0000ff">I agree with a physical or emotional change, disagree with the others.</font> <BR> <BR>His wife would be in the time of her life that signals the end of child-bearing and that could be an impetus for his restlessness.<font color="0000ff">I don&#39;t quite see it this way.</font> He closely associates the need to &#39;bring children into the world&#39; with his ability to &#39;take them out&#39;. Losing that option would make his wife less physically attractive, intimacy probably declined sharply, and they may sleep in separate rooms now - or they may have divorced. <font color="0000ff">A divorce is possible. I really believe that Josephine and JoeII Otero were murdered because BTK didn&#39;t expect them at the scene and couldn&#39;t take chances with witnesses. Remember that BTK did not harm the Vian children; I know BTK claims a phone call saved the lives of the kids, but BTK is a liar, all sociopaths are. Finally, if a ringing phone supposedly upset BTK, it means the phone lines were <b>not</b> cut.</font> <BR> <BR>At this point - I think he is harmless. He would use the knowledge that he is &#39;different&#39; from other SK&#39;s by the fact that he quit killing when the experts say a SK can not quit. It empowers him - and he justifies his actions in that. It makes him feel &#39;special&#39; in some way. He&#39;s not a SK - because he quit. That&#39;s what he thinks, anyway. <font color="0000ff">Experts who claim serials killers are incapable of stopping on their own are relying on information gathered a quarter of a century ago. Ed Kemper not only stopped, he turned himself in. Some serial killers can&#39;t stop, some can.</font> <BR> <BR>I doubt he feels guilty about his crimes - maybe he is sorry for the pain caused to family members - but he views his victims as &#34;collateral damage&#34; in some greater sphere.<font color="0000ff">I pretty much agree: BTK cares <i>nothing</i> about his crimes.</font> I&#39;ll bet he knows the Bible backwards and forewards. <font color="0000ff">I very much disagree as to BTK having an extensive knowledge of the Bible.</font>  <BR> <BR>He probably had some military training - as many have mentioned - but he did not fight in a war - probably used his time to get money for college - he started before his first youthful marriage - finished after that split.  <BR> <BR>He is an avid reader - writes well, English is his first language - and the only thing that reveals the real BTK in his correspondence - is his poetry. <font color="0000ff">English is his first language, yes. He is capable of writing prose well, in terms <BR>of vocabulary, syntax and grammar; his sloppy attempts to disguise this ability hurt him much more than they helped: they evince what he is, a liar and manipulator and criminal. BTK&#39;s poetry is a mishmash of vivid, often laughable, cliches;  is highly unoriginal and is designed to shock his betters. In the &#34;poetry&#34; thread, see all posts by Steve_Huff and Pax.</font> <BR> <BR>Not what he wrote - but &#39;because&#39; he wrote it. Poets are &#39;feelers&#39; - BTK feels things deeply. <font color="0000ff">I think BTK feels very little.</font>  <BR> <BR>BTK in his middle age years may have joined some &#34;control&#34; groups, PAC&#39;s, and the like. <font color="0000ff">I don&#39;t see this; BTK doesn&#39;t seem, to me, to be a joiner.</font> He is probably Republican, a white-collar job involving computers, and he would be attracted to groups that tried to, &#34;keep gays out of BoyScouts&#34;, or &#34;ban abortion&#34;, or &#34;close the borders&#34;, things of that nature as they are a harmless extension and outlet for his &#39;control&#39; aspect. <font color="0000ff">I tend to agree.</font> <BR> <BR>BTK may continue to reveal clues - but he may also &#34;move on&#34; - this cycle of life ending - he may try something else - in another area - or employer. I think it is a toss-up at this point. His kids would be adults - or close, by now, and with his wife&#39;s fertility ending - he is once again, looking for something to fill that &#39;void&#39;.<font color="0000ff">I agree that he has been trying to fill an internal void. This has been a lifelong pursuit and he has failed.</font>  <BR> <BR>So he is dangling the carrot - but he may not drop it. He knows the PD has nothing on him - and he is enjoying this time to &#39;rub it in&#39;.<font color="0000ff">Definitely. He&#39;s been dangling the carrot for thirty-one years.</font>  <BR> <BR>The bogus arrest a month or so ago - would have greatly pumped his ego. All his BS was actually believed <font color="0000ff">It wasn&#39;t believed by me. Or by a great many others but I appreciate your point.</font> - and the PD went after someone matching the clues BTK sent in. He probably laughed - or got a rush out of it - for days. <font color="0000ff">I don&#39;t doubt it.</font>  <BR> <BR>He feels invincible. <font color="0000ff">Yes. Frankly, he&#39;s still calling the shots. That&#39;s why none of the psychological ploys have worked. Of all things BTK may have laughed at, I&#39;d bet he laughed hardest at those promising him the highest degree of help. He is an absolutely worthless human being.</font>  <BR> <BR>Those are my, somewhat disconnected thoughts this early morning. <font color="0000ff">Apart from other posts, be sure to read Dr. kelleher&#39;s profile. It&#39;s imperative.</font> <BR>  <BR> <BR>   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
